# Data conversion between pebibyte and petabyte

Verifies direct data conversion between pebibyte and petabyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1PiB to 1.1258PB with a fractional coarser-to-finer scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5PiB yields 1.6888PB; backward, converting 1PB to 0.8881PiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5PB yields 1.3322PiB.

>>> source
const forward_whole: int = 1PiB
print(forward_whole->to(PB))
const forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5PiB
print(forward_fractional->to(PB))
const backward_whole: int = 1PB
print(backward_whole->to(PiB))
const backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5PB
print(backward_fractional->to(PiB))

<<< stdout
1.1258PB
1.6888PB
0.8881PiB
1.3322PiB

<<< stderr
